{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QBetaCKRecursionFromHabiroQDifference","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QBetaCKRecursionFromHabiroQDifference","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Powerset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Expand","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Reverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_bar_stable_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_bar_stable_general","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L332-L345","doc":"**General bar-stability — all `d > 1`** (eval form). Subsumes the explicit\n`cyclotomic_two/three/six_bar_stable` and `cyclotomic_prime_bar_stable`: for\nevery `n > 1`, `Φ_n` is self-reciprocal, `Φ_n(q⁻¹)·q^{φ(n)} = Φ_n(q)`, so\ndivisibility by `Φ_n` is invariant under the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`.\nDerived from `cyclotomic_self_reverse` via the reverse↔eval bridge\n`eval₂_reverse_mul_pow`, whose `[Invertible x]` hypothesis is supplied by\n`Units.invertible` — a unit, not a field inverse (§7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_self_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_self_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L285-L329","doc":"**General cyclotomic self-reciprocity (palindrome), all `n > 1`.** Over any\nintegral domain, `Φ_n` equals its own `reverse`. This is the full composite-`d`\ngeneralisation that Mathlib does not carry: it is proved by strong induction\non the divisor product `∏_{d ∣ n} Φ_d = Xⁿ − 1` (`prod_cyclotomic_eq_X_pow_sub_one`),\npeeling `d = 1` for the anti-palindrome sign and applying the IH on `1 < d < n`,\nthen cancelling the (nonzero) proper-divisor product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.reverse_X_pow_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.reverse_X_pow_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L271-L282","doc":"Auxiliary: `Xⁿ − 1` is anti-palindromic, `reverse (Xⁿ − 1) = 1 − Xⁿ`\n(so `cyclotomic 1 = X − 1` is bar-odd, the sign that seeds the induction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.reverse_finset_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.reverse_finset_prod","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L261-L268","doc":"Auxiliary: `reverse` is multiplicative across a `Finset` product over an\nintegral domain (`reverse_mul_of_domain` folded over the product). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_prime_bar_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_prime_bar_stable","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L238-L258","doc":"**General prime case** — subsumes `cyclotomic_two_bar_stable` and\n`cyclotomic_three_bar_stable` (and every other prime `p = 5, 7, 11, …`): for\nany prime `p`, `Φ_p` is self-reciprocal, `Φ_p(1/q)·q^{p-1} = Φ_p(q)`\n(`φ(p) = p-1`). Because `Φ_p = ∑_{i<p} X^i` (`cyclotomic_prime`), the identity\nis the index reflection `∑_{i<p} q^{p-1-i} = ∑_{i<p} q^i`\n(`Finset.sum_range_reflect`) — no per-prime computation needed. The remaining\ncomposite `d` (4, 6, 8, 9, …) need the general palindrome\n`reverse (cyclotomic d) = cyclotomic d`, which Mathlib does not yet carry;\n`cyclotomic_six_bar_stable` covers the one composite (`ζ_6`) the program uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_six_bar_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_six_bar_stable","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L228-L235","doc":"`Φ_6` is self-reciprocal: `Φ_6(q⁻¹)·q² = Φ_6(q)` (`φ(6)=2`) — the period-3/ζ₆\ncarrier whose bar-stability closes the period-3 constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_three_bar_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_three_bar_stable","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L219-L225","doc":"`Φ_3` is self-reciprocal: `Φ_3(q⁻¹)·q² = Φ_3(q)` (`φ(3)=2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_two_bar_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.cyclotomic_two_bar_stable","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L210-L216","doc":"`Φ_2` is self-reciprocal: `Φ_2(q⁻¹)·q = Φ_2(q)` (`φ(2)=1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L176-L182","doc":"Corollary of the parity-alternation theorem: for **even** `j` the recursion\ncoefficient `a_j = e_j` is bar-EVEN (`bar(a_j) = a_j`) — e.g. the bar-even\nseed rung `c_2 = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L167-L174","doc":"Corollary of the parity-alternation theorem: for **odd** `j` the recursion\ncoefficient `a_j = e_j` is bar-ODD (`bar(a_j) = -a_j`). These are the\nζ-carrying rungs of the ladder — the bar-odd `a_1 = -c_3`, and `a_3` (whose\nconcrete active-set ζ-content is ζ₂+ζ₆). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_bar_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_bar_parity","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L150-L165","doc":"**Parity-alternation theorem.**  For an involutive ring homomorphism\n`bar` under which every rate is **bar-odd** (`bar (r i) = - r i`), the\nelementary symmetric polynomials satisfy $\\overline{e_j} = (-1)^j e_j$.\nHence the recursion coefficient $a_j = e_j$ is bar-EVEN for even $j$ and\nbar-ODD for odd $j$ — they alternate bar-parity, independent of which\nmodes are active.  (The bar `q ↦ q⁻¹` of the fibre ring instantiates\n`bar`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm_neg","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L133-L148","doc":"**Negating the rates scales $e_j$ by $(-1)^j$.**  Each $j$-subset\nproduct picks up one sign per chosen element, i.e. $(-1)^j$, which\nfactors out of the sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.esymm","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L126-L131","doc":"**Elementary symmetric polynomial** $e_j(r)$ of a finite family\n`r : Fin n → R`: the sum, over $j$-element subsets, of the product of\nthe chosen rates.  The depth-$d$ recursion coefficient $a_j$ is\n$e_j$ of the active per-mode rates $r_\\lambda = (q-1)\\mu_\\lambda$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.applyRecursion_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.applyRecursion_linear","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L95-L107","doc":"**Recursion is linear in the history.**  Mixing two history vectors\n`h1, h2` and applying the recursion gives the same result as\napplying the recursion separately to each and adding.  Pure\nstructural identity — `Finset.sum_add_distrib` + `mul_add`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.applyRecursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.applyRecursion","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L78-L93","doc":"**Apply one step of the recursion.**\n\nGiven the last `depth` values of the $c_k$ sequence in\nchronological order (`history 0` is the most recent, `history\n(depth-1)` the oldest), output the next $c_k$ as the inner product\nof the kernel with the history.\n\nThe recursion is *purely linear* — no nonlinear iteration, no\nfixed-point search.  Once the kernel is identified (e.g. via the\ncategorical $f$-construction of `rem:markov-trace-inductive-limit`),\nevery $c_k$ for $k \\ge 2 + \\text{depth}$ follows by repeated\napplication from the seed values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.kernel","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.depth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.depth","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CKRecursion.CKRecursion","kind":"structure","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.lean#L54-L74","doc":"**Depth-$d$ linear recursion data for the $c_k$ precision-ladder\ncoefficients.**\n\nA fibre-level Habiro element $F$ satisfying a $q$-difference equation\nof depth $d$ — `F(q ξ) = R(q,ξ) · F(ξ)` with $R$ a Laurent polynomial\nof degree $d$ in $\\xi^{-1}$ — induces a depth-$d$ linear recursion\namong the Taylor coefficients of $F$.  The change-of-basis from\nthe Habiro `(u;u)_m` ring to the ladder $u^k$ inherits the same\ndepth, so the precision-ladder $c_k$ satisfy\n\n$$c_{k+1} = \\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} \\text{kernel}(j) \\cdot c_{k - j}.$$\n\nFields:\n* `depth` — order of the recursion (number of prior $c_k$ consumed)\n* `kernel : Fin depth → R` — the ring-valued recursion coefficients\n\nInstantiation requires specifying the kernel.  The seed value\n$c_2 = -1$ (PR #1602) is supplied to `applyRecursion` as input. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference","label":"prop:q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-recursion-from-habiro-q-difference.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}